; WAITKEY: a keypress pause, Phase 4's first "pause and wait on a live
; event" feature. Genuinely halts the script and waits for a real
; keypress in the entry box, then outputs its name as a word -- so this
; example only makes sense run from the actual app, not the headless
; test driver, where it's a silent no-op (returns the empty word
; immediately) instead of waiting forever.

TO drive
  MAKE "key WAITKEY
  IF :key = "Up [FD 20]
  IF :key = "Down [BK 20]
  IF :key = "Left [LT 15]
  IF :key = "Right [RT 15]
  IF NOT MEMBER? :key [Up Down Left Right] [STOP]
  drive
END

PRINT 'Press an arrow key to move the turtle -- any other key to stop.'
drive
PRINT "Stopped.
